{"name":"Magnesium","hex":"#c1c2c3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magnesium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The chemical element with an atomic number of 12. It is a light, easily flammable, silvery-white alkaline earth metal.","An atom of this element."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnesium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magnesium","blocks":[{"text":"Magnesium is a chemical element; it has symbol Mg and atomic number 12. It is a shiny gray metal having a low density, low melting point, and high chemical reactivity. Like the other alkaline earth metals, it occurs naturally only in combination with other elements and almost always has an oxidation state of +2. It reacts readily with air to form a thin passivation coating of magnesium oxide that inhibits further corrosion of the metal. The free metal burns with a brilliant-white light. The metal is obtained mainly by electrolysis of magnesium salts obtained from brine. It is less dense than aluminium and is used primarily as a component in strong and lightweight alloys that contain aluminium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/CSIRO_ScienceImage_2893_Crystalised_magnesium.jpg/330px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_2893_Crystalised_magnesium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnesium","wikidata":"Q660"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cold_rolling_of_Mg_and_Mg-1Al-0.1Ca.jpg/500px-Cold_rolling_of_Mg_and_Mg-1Al-0.1Ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cold_rolling_of_Mg_and_Mg-1Al-0.1Ca.jpg/500px-Cold_rolling_of_Mg_and_Mg-1Al-0.1Ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Magnesium is brittle, and fractures along shear bands when its thickness is reduced by only 10% by cold rolling (top). However, after alloying Mg with 1% Al and 0.1% Ca, its thickness could be reduced by 54% using the same process (bottom).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACold_rolling_of_Mg_and_Mg-1Al-0.1Ca.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg/500px-Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg/1280px-Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg/500px-Mg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Magnesium sheets and ingots","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMg_sheets_and_ingots.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg/500px-%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg/1280px-%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg/500px-%D9%85%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%A7%D8%AA_%D8%AF%D8%B1%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%AA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Iran